    "designMd": "# Design System: Folio3 Parking\n\n## 1. Visual Theme & Atmosphere\nA precise parking instrument for a working office. Employees, guards and administrators read this, and it should never feel like science fiction. Surfaces are near-black and tinted towards the accent blue in three steps. Depth comes from layered surfaces and 1px low-alpha hairlines, never from shadows or glow. Every number, plate, space code and time is set in monospace with tabular figures. Labels are small, uppercase and tightly controlled. One sharp blue does all the signalling, as thin lines, small fills and the focus ring.\n\n- **Density 7 – \"Cockpit Leaning\":** administrators sit at a desk all day, so tables are compact (36px rows), calm and fast to scan. Employee and holder views stay a step airier, but they use the same grid.\n- **Variance 4 – \"Offset, on grid\":** left-aligned headers, an asymmetric 8/4 split for a key figure beside its context, and strict column alignment. Nothing is centred for the sake of drama.\n- **Motion 7 – \"Fast and exact\":** numbers roll to their values, progress lines draw in, a code carries from a list into its detail, rows insert with a short shift, and one live dot breathes.\n\n**What we took from the field.** From **Tesla**: one colour on the primary action and sharp corners, everything else neutral. From **BMW**: a crisp, technical blue used with restraint. From **Ticketmaster**: blue actions and a pass/code view where one large key fact dominates. From **Ford**: a plain top bar, with no decoration in the chrome. We changed four field defaults on purpose: dark mode instead of light (a monitored, always-on entrance view); density raised from comfortable to dense (administrator signal); neutrals tinted cool-blue instead of pure; and monospace figures throughout instead of sans only.\n\n## 2. Color Palette & Roles\n- **Deep Bay** (#0A0E14): canvas, the lowest surface. Near-black tinted blue, never #000000.\n- **Bay Floor** (#10161F): surface step 2. Panels, table bodies, the side rail.\n- **Raised Deck** (#17202C): surface step 3. Popovers, sheets, selected rows, input fills.\n- **Hairline** (rgba(200,220,255,0.08)): 1px structural rules, table row dividers, panel edges.\n- **Hairline Strong** (rgba(200,220,255,0.16)): input borders, inset rules under section headers, hover row edge.\n- **Instrument White** (#E6ECF4): primary text and key figures.\n- **Gauge Grey** (#8C98A8): secondary text, metadata, column headers.\n- **Dim Scale** (#5B6676): disabled text, placeholder, axis ticks.\n- **Signal Blue** (#3F7FD8): the single accent. Primary button fill (with Deep Bay ink for 4.7:1 contrast), active tab indicator, progress lines, the selected-row left rule, links and the 2px focus ring. Saturation is about 65%. It never glows.\n- **Signal Blue Wash** (rgba(63,127,216,0.12)): selected-row and pressed-row tint only.\n- **Status: Cleared** (#3FB37F): verified entry, active vehicle, success. Used as a 6px dot plus a text label, never as a large fill.\n- **Status: Refused** (#E5484D): failed verification, destructive confirm, inline errors.\n- **Status: Hold** (#D9A23A): pending, manual check needed, warnings.\n\nStatus colours appear only where a state is being reported. They are never decoration.\n\n## 3. Typography Rules\n- **Display / Headings:** IBM Plex Sans, weight 600 for page titles (clamp(1.375rem, 1.1rem + 0.8vw, 1.75rem), tracking −0.02em) and weight 500 for section heads (1rem). Hierarchy comes from weight and colour, not size.\n- **Body:** IBM Plex Sans 400, 0.875rem in tables and 0.9375rem in reading text, line-height 1.55, max 65ch.\n- **Mono:** IBM Plex Mono with `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` for every number, plate, space code, floor, date, time, count and email address in a data cell. Key figures (a live count, a space code on a pass) use Mono 500 at clamp(2.5rem, 2rem + 2vw, 3.5rem), tracking −0.03em.\n- **Labels:** Plex Sans 500, 0.6875rem, UPPERCASE, tracking +0.08em, Gauge Grey.\n- **Craft:** curly quotes, en dash for ranges (09:00–18:00), a real ellipsis, dates in the format \"Tue 14 Oct 2025\" and 24-hour time. The page's one deliberate contrast is case: uppercase labels against sentence-case headings.\n- **Banned:** Inter, serif fonts of any kind, and the AI-default list in §10 of the skill.\n\n## 4. Component Stylings\n- **Buttons:** 2px radius, 36px tall (44px tap area on touch). Primary: Signal Blue fill with Deep Bay text, weight 500, and a verb specific to the action. Secondary: transparent with a Hairline Strong border and Instrument White text. Destructive: Refused text with a Refused 1px border, filled only in the confirm step. Press is `scale(0.97)` at 90ms. Never a glow, gradient or pulse.\n- **Panels instead of cards:** Bay Floor surfaces with a 1px Hairline edge and an inset 1px rule under the header. No shadows. Raised Deck marks the one level above (menus, sheets, dialogs), and dialogs alone get a single shadow, `0 12px 32px rgba(4,8,14,0.6)`.\n- **Tables:** 36px rows, Hairline dividers, uppercase label headers, figures right-aligned in Mono. Hovering a row tints it with rgba(200,220,255,0.03). A selected row gets Signal Blue Wash plus a 2px Signal Blue left rule. Headers are sticky, and sorting is shown by a small chevron in Gauge Grey that turns blue when active.\n- **Status cell:** a 6px dot plus an uppercase label in the status colour. Never a pill with a tinted background.\n- **Key-figure block:** a large Mono figure, an uppercase label above it and one line of context below. It sits in the 8-column side of an 8/4 split, never in a row of equal KPI tiles.\n- **Inputs:** label above, helper or error below in 0.75rem. Raised Deck fill, Hairline Strong border, 2px radius. Focus is a 2px Signal Blue outline at 2px offset. Plate and code inputs use Mono uppercase. No floating labels.\n- **Tabs / segmented controls:** text labels with a 2px Signal Blue underline indicator that slides between tabs.\n- **Loaders:** skeleton bars matching the row and figure dimensions, with a shimmer of 4% opacity. No spinners.\n- **Empty states:** a short, specific sentence that says how to fill the view, plus one action button. The illustration is a thin-line plate outline or a bay outline in Hairline Strong.\n- **Errors:** inline beneath the field or at the top of the panel, with a Refused rule on the left and a plain explanation of what to do next. Retry is a secondary button.\n\n## 5. Layout Principles\n- 12-column CSS grid, max-width 1440px, 24px gutters. Admin views have a 232px left rail on Bay Floor with text-only navigation, set in uppercase labels with no icons. Employee views have a plain top bar.\n- Content starts at column 1 and aligns to the grid. The asymmetric 8/4 split puts a figure or primary panel on the left and context or actions on the right.\n- Section rhythm varies: a key-figure band, then a dense table, then a narrow settings column (max 640px).\n- Full-height views use `min-h-[100dvh]`. No overlapping or absolutely stacked content.\n- **Responsive:** below 768px everything collapses to a single column, the rail becomes a top bar with a menu sheet, and tables become stacked row blocks that keep the Mono figures. Horizontal page scroll is never allowed. Tap targets are at least 44px. Section gaps use clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem).\n\n## 6. Motion & Interaction\nMotion is fast and exact, and it carries meaning. Numbers roll to their real value, progress and utilisation lines draw in, a code carries from its list row into its detail, inserted rows shift in by 8px, and exactly one live indicator breathes. Only transform and opacity are animated, plus clip-path on draw-in lines. The full system is in §9.\n\n## 7. Anti-Patterns (Banned)\n- No emojis. No Inter or serif fonts. No pure black (#000000).\n- No glow, neon, outer shadows on buttons, gradient blobs, aurora, glassmorphism or backdrop blur, and no purple-to-blue gradients.\n- No rows of equal KPI cards with sparklines and \"+12%\". No 3-equal-card rows. No bento grid of equal tiles.\n- No pill badges, sparkle icons or icons on every nav item.\n- No \"Get started\" or AI clichés (\"Seamless\", \"Elevate\", \"Next-Gen\"). No placeholder names or round fake numbers.\n- No spinners, bouncing, pulsing buttons, typewriter text, parallax, fly-ins, or the same fade-up on every section.\n- No custom cursors and no overlapping elements.\n\n## 8. Voice & Font Rationale\n- **Voice:** exact, watchful, calm.\n- **Display:** IBM Plex Sans. Its engineered, slightly mechanical forms (squared curves, a distinct `a` and `g`) read like instrument labelling, not marketing. Fallback: Hanken Grotesk.\n- **Body / Mono:** IBM Plex Sans with IBM Plex Mono. They come from one family, so plates, codes and times sit on the same metrics as the prose, and Mono's slashed zero keeps plate characters unambiguous.\n\n## 9. Motion System\n- **Tokens:** `--dur-instant: 90ms; --dur-quick: 160ms; --dur-base: 260ms; --dur-slow: 420ms; --dur-scene: 760ms; --ease-out: cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1); --ease-in: cubic-bezier(0.7,0,0.84,0); --ease-inout: cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1); --ease-spring: linear(0, 0.009, 0.035 2.1%, 0.141, 0.281 6.7%, 0.723 12.9%, 0.938 16.7%, 1.017, 1.077 21.4%, 1.121 24%, 1.149 27%, 1.159, 1.154 33%, 1.051 43.2%, 1.013 49.5%, 0.996 57%, 1.001 72%, 1); --travel: 8px`. Exits use about 70% of the entrance duration with `--ease-in`.\n- **Entrance:** the page title, then the key figure, then the first panel reveal as opacity 0→1 with an 8px rise, staggered 60ms. The key figure rolls from 0 to its value over 600ms with `--ease-out`. Total time is under 760ms.\n- **Scroll-linked:** utilisation and progress bars draw in once with `clip-path: inset(0 100% 0 0)` → `inset(0)` and `animation-timeline: view(); animation-range: entry 0% entry 40%`, so the bar shows the share being reported. They never replay.\n- **Interaction feedback:** buttons press at scale(0.97) over 90ms. A text link's underline draws from the left with scaleX 0→1 at 160ms. A row hover tints the background at 160ms, and its trailing arrow nudges 3px. Focus-visible shows the 2px Signal Blue outline instantly.\n- **State transitions:** the tab indicator slides between tabs over 260ms with `--ease-inout`. Accordions use `grid-template-rows: 0fr→1fr` over 260ms. New rows insert with opacity plus an 8px shift over 160ms, and the inserted row holds a Signal Blue Wash that fades out over 1.2s. Sheets slide up over 420ms with `--ease-out` while the backdrop fades to 40%.\n- **Ambient (max 1):** the live status dot next to a live-updating feed or count breathes, opacity 1→0.55 and scale 1→1.25 on a 6px dot, on a 6s `--ease-inout` infinite cycle. Nothing else loops.\n- **Signature moment, \"Code carry\":** a space or plate code in a list row shares `view-transition-name: code-[id]` with the large Mono code on its detail or pass view, so it travels and scales there over 420ms with `--ease-out` through the View Transitions API. Where the API is unavailable, it falls back to a 160ms cross-fade.\n- **Reduced motion:** with `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, entrances become instant opacity changes, numbers show their final value, draw-ins appear complete, the breathing dot is static, view transitions become a 120ms fade, and no content waits on an animation.\n\n```css\n:root{--dur-instant:90ms;--dur-quick:160ms;--dur-base:260ms;--dur-slow:420ms;--dur-scene:760ms;\n--ease-out:cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1);--ease-in:cubic-bezier(0.7,0,0.84,0);--ease-inout:cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1);--travel:8px}\n@keyframes rise{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(var(--travel))}to{opacity:1;transform:none}}\n@keyframes draw{from{clip-path:inset(0 100% 0 0)}to{clip-path:inset(0)}}\n@keyframes breathe{0%,100%{opacity:1;transform:scale(1)}50%{opacity:.55;transform:scale(1.25)}}\n@keyframes row-in{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(-8px)}to{opacity:1;transform:none}}\n.reveal{animation:rise var(--dur-slow) var(--ease-out) both}\n.bar-fill{animation:draw var(--dur-slow) var(--ease-out) both;animation-timeline:view();animation-range:entry 0% entry 40%}\n.live-dot{width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:#3FB37F;animation:breathe 6s var(--ease-inout) infinite}\n.row-new{animation:row-in var(--dur-quick) var(--ease-out) both}\n::view-transition-group(*){animation-duration:var(--dur-slow);animation-timing-function:var(--ease-out)}\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{animation:none!important;transition:opacity 120ms linear!important}::view-transition-group(*){animation-duration:120ms}}\n```\n\n## 10. Component Substitutions\n- 4 KPI cards with sparklines → one Mono key figure with a context line, followed by a dense sortable table.\n- Pill status badges → a 6px dot plus an uppercase label.\n- Icon-led navigation → a text-only uppercase rail.\n- Shadow-lifted cards → layered Bay Floor / Raised Deck surfaces with hairlines.\n- Generic \"Get started\" CTAs → verbs specific to each action.\n- Spinners → dimension-matched skeletons.\n- Default shadcn zinc and 0.5rem radius → a 2px sharp radius and a blue offset focus ring.\n\n## 11. Human Fingerprint\n- **Unexpected decision:** plate and space codes are always set in a Mono \"plate frame\", with a 1px Hairline Strong border, 2px radius, 2px 6px padding and uppercase letters, wherever they appear. Everything the parking world identifies by a code therefore looks like a physical tag, and the same frame is what the signature motion carries.\n- **Radius / elevation / grid:** sharp family, 2px on everything (inner elements 0–2px). Two elevation levels: tint steps everywhere, and one shadow for dialogs only. 12-column grid, 1440px max-width, 24px gutters.\n- **Image treatment / icons:** no photography in the chrome. Any illustration is thin line art in Hairline Strong. Lucide icons at stroke 1.25, 16px only, used only for status, sort, close and external links.\n",
